./packages/plugin-detail/CHANGELOG.md:1191:  The button is icon-only: its sole child was a lucide `X`, with no text, `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby` or `title`. lucide-react excludes childless, a11y-prop-less icons from the accessibility tree (it defaults them to `aria-hidden="true"`), so the button had no name source at all and its computed accessible name was the empty string — a screen reader announced a nameless "button". Unlike the placeholder case in #3381 there was no browser-side fallback to soften it: the name was empty in every implementation. WCAG 4.1.2 / 2.4.6.
