./packages/plugin-grid/CHANGELOG.md:869:  One component answered one question two ways. `ObjectGrid` seeded its density state with `schema.rowHeight ?? 'compact'`, so an ABSENT `rowHeight` landed on `compact` while an OFF-SPEC one skipped every arm of the density ternaries and came out at their terminal `else` — the `medium` styling. That is the absent-vs-off-spec split objectui#4440 removed from `ListView`, and it made a standalone grid the third answer to a question the rest of the system had already settled: `@object-ui/core`'s `rowHeightToDensityMode` abstains for an off-spec value, the `@object-ui/react` spec bridge abstains, and `ListView` defaults the abstention to `compact`. Off-spec now renders exactly like absent, everywhere.
